<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">State Counsellor of Myanmar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2016–2021</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The State Counsellor of Myanmar was a post created in April 2016 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aung-san-suu-kyi">Aung San Suu Kyi</a>, who was barred from the presidency by the 2008 constitution because her sons held foreign citizenship. Comparable to a prime minister, it gave her leadership of the government and the right to advise the president and parliament. The office ended with the military coup of 2021.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/state-counsellor-of-myanmar.jpg" alt="State Counsellor of Myanmar" width="320" height="262" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:State seal of Myanmar (1974-1988).svg: User:Пакко. Derivative work: Gringer (talk). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Variant_of_the_State_seal_of_Myanmar_(2011-2025).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
